# X86-PHALANX — all of standalone x86_64 emit-x86

File: openOODA/audit/x86_phalanx.oot
Owner named this backend. C emit + gcc stays the everyday path.
AArch64 stays residual unless the owner names it.
C/LLVM rebuilds own product oodac/oodac; re-pin overlay for x86 proof.
Do not edit the public site (Grok 2). Do not edit c_emit*, llvm*, wasm*.

## 0. Disk now

  Files: oodac/x86_emit.oo plus fold/sys/harv/walk/alu/ctl/bind/span/fn
  and frame/rsi/str/greet (each ≤256). Harvest write-and-exit: greet fold,
  const ALU + - * / %, paren, let/mut, == != > < <= >= if, else-if,
  if true/false, mix concat and mix-paren. Leftover-plus-print ERRs even
  when another print was harvested (hostile other; leftover_ident).
  Locks: scripts/x86_*_smoke.oo. Cycle C on disk: two-arg snd lea rdi+rsi,
  call snd, mov %rsi,%rax, as+ld hi (x86_snd_smoke.oo). Identity frame
  push %rbp / mov %rsp,%rbp / pop %rbp (x86_frame_smoke.oo). .bss bump
  concat cat yy+zz → yyzz via .skip 4096 and .Lcpy (x86_cat_smoke.oo).
  Overflow 2048+2048+1 ERR x86 buf no _start (x86_buf_ovf_smoke.oo).
  while/for leftover ERR, no silent once (x86_while_smoke.oo). greet
  real call println(greet("World")) → Hello, World! with call greet and
  lea .Lnm %rdi (x86_greet_call_smoke.oo). hello.oo fold still has no
  call greet. Wiring: fold, then SysV, then harvest. as+ld, no gcc, no
  chs_rt. Host x86_64. Overlay ELF 1755696 at
  /tmp/ooda-x86-ovl-handoff/oodac and product oodac/oodac. Isolated
  rebuild pin afb96e99 + x86 overlay, OK_PURE_MULTI. Pin: cp overlay to
  oodac/oodac.new; mv -f onto oodac/oodac. Foreign C/LLVM rebuilds
  overwrite product oodac/oodac; re-pin before smokes. C emit+gcc
  remains the everyday path. Cycle A proved. Cycle B harvest on disk.
  Do not claim the x86 backend complete.

## 1. All of x86 (staircase)

  Cycle A — greet fold (first ship)
    fixtures/hello.oo: greet("openOODA Developer") + concat + println(message).
    emit-x86 + as + ld prints `Hello, openOODA Developer!` and exits 0.
    OPEN-69 literal lock stays green.
    How: const-fold greet(STRING) + "Hello, "+name+"!" into one rodata string.
    Not a general string heap.

  Cycle B — int floor
    let x: Int, +, -, *, if, while, println of a folded int or a second
    literal. Named fixture. as+ld runs. No libc.

  Cycle C — real calls
    User fn with String or Int args. SysV: rdi, rsi, stack frame,
    rip-relative lea. greet actually calls, then concat in a .bss bump
    (cap 4096). Overflow: ERR x86 buf, no .s body.

  Cycle D — stay residual unless named
    AArch64, import graphs, Result/Option match, List, SECRET beyond
    current println sink, libc, gcc, chs_rt.

  Do not start B until A is proved. Do not start C until B is proved.

## 2. Cycle A ship bar

  From ooda/ on a compiler that includes the new x86_*.oo files:
    ./oodac/oodac emit-x86 fixtures/hello.oo > /tmp/hello.s
    as --64 -o /tmp/hello.o /tmp/hello.s
    ld -o /tmp/hello.bin /tmp/hello.o
    /tmp/hello.bin
  stdout is exactly `Hello, openOODA Developer!` plus newline. exit 0.
  .s has _start and main. No #include, no chs_rt, no int main(.
  open69_hello.oo still prints Hello.
  empty source: ERR x86_emit empty, exit 1.
  SECRET println still refuses (call check_secret_println_sinks only;
  do not edit c_emit_secret_check.oo).

## 3. Frozen helpers (Cycle A)

  Keep:
    pub fn x86_emit_stream(src: String)
    fn x86_ascii_esc(s: String) -> String
    fn x86_collect_prints(toks: List[String]) -> List[String]
    fn x86_emit_linux64(msgs: List[String])

  Add (DE2 owns the body):
    pub fn x86_fold_hello(src: String) -> String
  Return the folded greet+concat message when src matches hello.oo shape
  (fn greet(name) returns "Hello, " + name + "!", main does
  let message = greet("..."); println(message)).
  Return "" otherwise. Empty means keep today's literal-only path.

  DE1: if x86_fold_hello is non-empty, emit that one string via
  x86_emit_linux64. Else x86_collect_prints as today.

