## 5. Subagent waves

  Wave 1 (builders + harness fixtures) — parallel
    DE1, DE2, RT, HARN (write x86_hello_smoke; do not flip open69 yet)
  Wave 2 (adversarial) — after Wave 1 files exist
    PV1, PV2, SEC, MEM
  Wave 3 (prove + boards) — after one side rebuild
    INT, HYG, DOCS, COORD rollup

  Isolation: none. Disjoint files. No worktree.
  Rebuild: side binary only, oodac/oodac.x86
    PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1 only if the host cannot check new helpers.
    Do not write oodac/oodac.
  Smokes that must run emit-x86 prefer ./oodac/oodac.x86 if executable,
  else ./oodac/oodac.

  Anti-pattern: two agents on the same stuck as/ld failure.

## 6. Forbidden

  No .py .sh .md .js.
  No c_emit*.oo (including c_emit_secret_check.oo).
  No llvm_emit*.oo. No wasm_emit*.oo.
  No lex/parse/check/tc. No main.oo. No cli_emit.oo. No cli_build.oo.
  No runtime/chs_rt*.c.
  No guide/ or registry HTML.
  Do not copy bin/ooda onto oodac/oodac.
  Do not claim AArch64. Do not retire C emit + gcc.

## 7. Proof commands (Cycle A)

  From ooda/:
    ./oodac/oodac.x86 emit-x86 fixtures/hello.oo > .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/x86_hello.s
    as --64 -o .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/x86_hello.o .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/x86_hello.s
    ld -o .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/x86_hello.bin .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/x86_hello.o
    .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/x86_hello.bin
  Existing:
    ./bin/ooda run scripts/open69_x86_smoke.oo
  New:
    ./bin/ooda run scripts/x86_hello_smoke.oo
    ./bin/ooda run scripts/x86_phalanx_int.oo

## 8. Later cycles (not Wave 1)

  Cycle B files (after A): x86_emit_expr.oo, x86_emit_ctrl.oo.
    New 12-role pass. Same forbidden list. New fixtures, new smokes.
  Cycle C files (after B): x86_emit_fn.oo, x86_emit_str.oo, x86_emit_frame.oo.
    MEM owns the 4096 bump cap. RT owns SysV moves.
  Cycle D: owner must name AArch64 or imports.

## 9. Why this split

  emit-x86 harvests consts and emits SysV calls. Not a backend.
  Cycle A matches the WASM print-lit ship: one named program, real bytes,
  as+ld (not wasmtime). Fold is honest: hello.oo is const.
  Cycle B harvests ALU/if/let/mix. Cycle C proved rdi/rsi/frame/bump/greet-call.
  Do not claim libc or AArch64.

